{"status":"success","data":[{"siteid":33301,"sitename":"Lusvatnet","sitedescription":"Small oval lake. Physiography: small cirque glacier that drained into Lusvatnet during the\r\nLateglacial. Surrounding vegetation: Open birch woodland dominated by Betula pubescens ssp. tortuosa and with a predominantly ericaceous or tall-fern-dominated understory clothes the steep lower slopes. Above the tree-line, the vegetation is composed of ericaceous dwarf-shrubs and grasses on sheltered slopes, open grass-heath on exposed ridges, and cliff vegetation around the head of the lake where several arctic-alpine and montane species occur.","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[15.56667,69.06667]}","altitude":30,"recdatecreated":"2025-04-11T07:15:25.000Z","collectionunits":[{"handle":"LUSVATN","datasets":[{"datasetid":62037,"datasettype":"pollen"}],"collectionunit":"core LUP207","collectionunitid":45055,"collectionunittype":"Core"}]}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}